Built by openprinthq-desktops (apps/bambustudio): the steps that restyle linuxserver.io's Bambu Studio image
for OpenPrintHQ. The repository holds no copy of that image, of its source or of Bambu Studio. The image built
contains the works below, each under its own licence, which the repository and the image keep.

linuxserver.io docker-bambustudio
  https://github.com/linuxserver/docker-bambustudio
  Copyright (C) linuxserver.io. GNU General Public License, version 3 (LICENSE).
  The image's base, its start-up scripts, its window manager settings (defaults/labwc.xml) and its web server
  set-up (etc/s6-overlay/s6-rc.d/init-nginx/run) are linuxserver.io's; common/restyle.py changes the last two
  as described in it. The repository's own files are offered under the same licence, GPL-3.0 (LICENSE).

Selkies
  https://github.com/selkies-project/selkies
  The web desktop and its dashboard (usr/share/selkies), Mozilla Public License 2.0 as published with it.
  The OpenPrintHQ dashboard is a copy of Selkies' own with one stylesheet added; Selkies' files are not changed.

Bambu Studio
  https://github.com/bambulab/BambuStudio
  Copyright (C) Bambu Lab. GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 (LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt).
  Bambu Studio is used as linuxserver.io ships it. apps/bambustudio/convert.py changes colour and font values
  in five of its web resource files (resources/web/guide/css/dark.css, guide/css/common.css,
  homepage3/css/dark.css, homepage3/css/common.css, homepage3/css/left.css); those files, as changed, stay
  under the AGPL-3.0, and their source is the upstream file and the change in convert.py. Bambu Studio's
  source is at the address above, at the tag of the version named in apps/bambustudio/upstream.env.

Fonts
  Manrope, Sora and JetBrains Mono, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (the licence files are in the image next to the
  fonts, usr/share/selkies/artisanhub-dashboard/ahi/fonts).
